The Government may implement the following projects to protect fundamental rights and interests of users:
Providing information on the information security industry to users and education of users;
Fact-finding research as to whether guidelines for protection of users under Article 36 are complied with;
Education concerning the protection of users intended for information security enterprises;
Providing support to institutions or organizations aiming at protecting users;
Formulating and implementing measures for preventing loss of users and providing users with relief;
Formulating and implementing other measures for protecting rights and interests of users.
The Government shall formulate and implement necessary measures so that persons difficult to freely approach or use information security products or services due to economical, regional, physical or social circumstances can use information security products or services in a convenient manner.

